<title>UK: European cotton enquiry slow.</title>
<headline>European cotton enquiry slow.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spinner enquiry in Europe cotton markets was at a low ebb in the absence of new stimulus, traders said.</p>
<p>However, occasional buying interest was noted, particularly in Portugal and Italy where attention was directed to competitively priced autumn shipment offers of Greek and Spanish medium/better qualities.</p>
<p>Turkey also reported a sustained latent buying interest in U.S. descriptions.</p>
<p>Eastern Europe was dull apart from isolated price testing enquiries for such cottons as Central Asian and American Pima.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
